<!-- V6f PROBE ORDER (PREREG_V6C_LATE_JOINER_2026-09-15.md AMENDMENT 5, 2026-09-15).
     R5 WITH THE COMPANY AND TANK TASKS REMOVED - T_R5_PL1 only, on 1222.MechPlt~PXY.

     WHY. V6d and V6e both stopped the back end the moment the R5 order dispatched, on
     fixtures with and without nav data. The level-4 console says why the load is not equal
     across the three tasks: T_R5_CO1, the COMPANY task on a composed unit, FANS OUT to
     1141/1142/1143.MechPlt, and 16 members begin building movement trees in the same second
     (16 distinct emitters each creating a 'Loop to stall for replanning' node between
     t=30.2 and t=30.7). T_R5_PL1 is one platoon; T_R5_TK1 is one entity - and the tank's
     taskee is the ONLY object in V6e that moved at all (~299 m) before the engine seized.

     So this order REMOVES THE SUSPECT and keeps the smallest ground move that still
     exercises maneuver-in-formation and off-road path planning:
       HIT  (back end survives) -> the company fan-out is the trigger; V6g runs the company
                                   task ALONE to confirm it from the other side.
       MISS (back end stops, ws climbing ~2 GB/min as in V6d/V6e) -> a single platoon move is
                                   enough, and the trigger is the move or the composition
                                   itself, not the fan-out.

     Generated from data/R5_UnitMove_Order.xml by removing the 2nd and 3rd <Task> blocks.
     Nothing else is edited - same OrderID, same routes, same ROE, same performing entity.
-->
